{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "10276",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10276",
  "key": "AIN-47",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Ensured] Strengthen canonical data models and database integrity",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Priority: foundational work for insurer pilot and capital release. Review date: 2026-11-01. Improve current models additively; this epic owns schema architecture and enforcement, while existing domain epics own business workflows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Problem and evidence"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Current models span identity/organizations, canonical submissions, ModelRun/PricingVersion, quote/binding snapshots, commercial SQL ledgers, capital models and subscriptions. Party roles, actor identity, currency, provenance and financial lifecycle states are represented differently. Several monetary models lack explicit currency; posting organization is not a payer/payee identity. JSONB extensions and service-local ownership are intentional and must remain supported."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Outcomes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A reviewed as-is/to-be entity relationship model and field dictionary identifies tenant ownership, authoritative writers, parties, monetary units and version references."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Database-enforced integrity, validated versioned extensions and explicit cross-service contracts prevent malformed or contradictory records."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Rebuildable read projections, measured indexes and safe staged migrations support operations without losing historical evidence."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing domain delivery \u2014 link, do not duplicate"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AIN-18 owns financial revision behavior; AIN-20/21 pricing availability and atomicity; AIN-22 loss experience; AIN-26 binding handoff; AIN-29 beneficiary controls; AIN-34 party subledger; AIN-35 money/currency semantics; AIN-36 settlement; AIN-37 premium splits; AIN-38/39/40 claims and reversals; AIN-43/44 billing; AIN-45/46 financial validation and coverage. Their existing parents remain unchanged. Schema tasks here provide explicit implementation contracts to those tickets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Definition of done"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Approved schema decisions identify cardinalities, keys, tenant boundaries, nullable/unknown semantics, uniqueness, lifecycle rules and ownership."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Additive migrations and backfills pass on representative legacy fixtures; unresolved values are quarantined rather than guessed."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Schema/constraint and cross-version compatibility checks run in CI; documented query plans meet agreed staging workloads."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Existing tenant isolation, org-editable risk-class schemas, immutable evidence and historical replay remain intact."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sequencing"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Start with entity/ownership mapping. Agree party, money and revision semantics with AIN-34, AIN-35 and AIN-18. Then implement constraints, extension contracts and cross-service events. Validate migrations and query projections before cutover. No production database change is authorized or performed by creating this epic."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Roadmap priority 2 of 14 open epics. One developer, two-week sprints"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S02 Canonical ownership contracts: AIN-48"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S03 Database integrity and CI: AIN-49, AIN-55"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S04 Flexible schema and revision contracts: AIN-50, AIN-51"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S12 Indexed rebuildable projections: AIN-53"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S15 Remaining financial identity adapters: AIN-59"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "S54 Legacy migration rehearsal: AIN-54"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Historical epic-level Blocks links remain intact as delivery/release constraints. Readiness for a child uses the named prerequisite milestone, not completion of every late child of a foundational epic. AIN-1 provides build/staging foundations early and full integration/restore late; AIN-47 contracts are early and legacy cutover late. No epic is closed at an early milestone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Epic completion requires every original criterion, unfinished child/subtask and required dependency, including criteria not exhausted by the sprint issue titles. Early foundation milestones do not close this epic. Full backlog mapping and gate register are recorded on AIN-12 and in TASK_HANDOFF.md."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
